{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update","id":1524819,"title":"Vampire Bloodlines update","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-31T10:18:38-07:00","id":1524819,"title":"Vampire Bloodlines update","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/uwXf5nMa-UI\" data-code=\"uwXf5nMa-UI\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/uwXf5nMa-UI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> From TVtropes' <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Tropers/Lavaeolus\" target=\"_blank\">Lavaeolus</a>\u200b<br /> <br /> They reveal some more of the story and show off a bit of dialogue. Some notes:<ul><li><b>We play as Phyre</b>, an elder vampire who is pointedly not a blank slate. Their gender and clan is customisable, though, and apparently you get some choice over what they've done in their background.</li> <li><b>You're voiced</b>, and indeed, looking at the gameplay, rather than choosing between lines of dialogue it looks like you choose between various approaches (e.g. one dialogue lets you choose &quot;Remind him who you are&quot; or &quot;Show concern for his wellbeing&quot;).</li> <li><b>She hears the voice of Fabien</b>, a modern thinblood from Seattle. He's trapped in her body and their relationship might grow in different ways, although it seems initially... strained. Phyre has a mark on their hand, which seems related to all this.</li> <li><b>Outfits matter?</b> Apparently you can choose your outfit and they'll have an effect on dialogue and narrative. I don't know how important this will be.</li> <li><b>They'll be revealing the playable clans &quot;soon&quot;.</b> According to <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/rpg-and-narrative-stream\" target=\"_blank\">an accompanying post<img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/external_link.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/external_link.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/external_link.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a>, there'll be four clans playable at launch and the first will be revealed next week. Two clans will be in DLC. &quot;Some of the clans will be familiar to Bloodlines players, but some will surprise!&quot;</li> </ul>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T10:24:44-07:00","id":1524820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update#post1524819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>They'll be revealing the playable clans &quot;soon&quot;.</b> According to <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/rpg-and-narrative-stream\" target=\"_blank\">an accompanying post<img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/external_link.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/external_link.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/external_link.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a>, there'll be four clans playable at launch and the first will be revealed next week. Two clans will be in DLC. &quot;Some of the clans will be familiar to Bloodlines players, but some will surprise!&quot;[/LIST]\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh come on...! Seriously...?! sigh Well, I guess, it wouldn't be a real AAA modern game if they didn't nickel &amp; dime you with DLC...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T10:48:13-07:00","id":1524821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update#post1524819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[ &quot;Some of the clans will be familiar to Bloodlines players, but some will surprise!&quot;<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The Brujah, Gangrel, Malkavian,Nosferatu, Ventrue, Toreador and Tremere were playable<br /> The Giovanni had a whole chapter<br /> Andrei was a Tzimisce (and The Sheriff was probably a Nagloper), Pisha was a Nagaraja, the Gargoyle... was a Gargoyle<br /> We had a few Kuei-jin<br /> \u200b<br /> So what remains are and we are &quot;not familiar with&quot;:<br /> Lasombra<br /> Ravnos<br /> Banu Haqim<br /> Salubri<br /> Followers of Set<br /> Hecata, maybe?<br /> <br /> I wonder what will be the &quot;surprise&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T11:47:15-07:00","id":1524823,"title":"","content":"4 clans playable at launch and 2 DLC? So not even all 7 of the original clans will be playable? That's a bit disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T12:22:53-07:00","id":1524826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]<b>She hears the voice of Fabien</b>, a modern thinblood from Seattle. He's trapped in her body and their relationship might grow in different ways, although it seems initially... strained. Phyre has a mark on their hand, which seems related to all this.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>Ah, someone was a fan of Cyberpunk and Johny Silverhand I see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T14:28:04-07:00","id":1524840,"title":"","content":"I've now watched the video and... oh man, if those sneak peeks are any indication this will be a rough ride. That female VA for Phyre is bad. I assume it's due to bad direction (getting told to sound ancient and disinterested) but the result is that she just sounds flat. The cuts between characters as they say lines also feel badly timed as well as facial animations that are &quot;okay&quot;, I would say. This is the sort of quality I would expect from a mid-tier-game. It certainly isn't AAA-type stuff (which makes the DLC-stuff just more insulting).<br /> <br /> Also, this contradicts what was said but considering just how many times it came up: This game absolutely has a &quot;Paragon/Renegade&quot;-esque system. It's 2023. Bringing up Mass Effect that much isn't a coincidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T16:41:46-07:00","id":1524850,"title":"","content":"I'm still not happy it has an Elder protagonist.<br /> <br /> Elders are gross and mean.<br /> <br /> NOT LIKE ANARCHS!<br /> <br /> Who are just mean or gross but not both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T17:30:37-07:00","id":1524851,"title":"","content":"There are Elder Anarchs :P<br /> <br /> The Elder with a thin-blood magically forced into their head is one of the few good things I heard in all this. Not forcing people into the zero-to-hero progression, and creating two main characters that highlight a lot of the conflicts in the setting with a setup that doesn't require any existing setting knowledge is a decent concept.<br /> <br /> I don't see the choppiness of the dialogue as a red flag.. it's post-alpha. The whole point of moving into beta is taking a game that mostly works, and polishing it into a game that's actually good<br /> <br /> Resonance is a V5 thing, so it's in the game, neutral issue. Gamifying clothing feels silly. I get the idea, but I don't see a way to make it fun instead of just being necessary to maximize your odds in different scenarios.<br /> <br /> The DLC Clans is a horrible move considering the existing resentment of V5 skipping lots of them for corebook inclusion.<br /> <br /> &quot;Phyre&quot; is a flashback of the bad sorts to 90s edginess. &quot;Angst McEdgelord&quot; would at least be funny. Why would an Elder call themselves this? They're too old to give a shit about how it &quot;looks cool&quot; to use &quot;ph&quot; and &quot;y&quot; instead of just saying &quot;fire.&quot; Does the protagonist identify deeply for some reason with rocks that have highly differentiated mineral grain structures caused by differential cooling? Unisex homophones exist in almost every culture and language that could have allowed for something old fashioned by not require twice the line reading on the voice actors.<br /> <br /> It's painfully limited as a teaser of game play. &quot;We have a decent dialogue tree UI!&quot; is not the first thing on gamers' minds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T17:32:18-07:00","id":1524852,"title":"","content":"Damn edit flag.<br /> <br /> My reactions will reappear when they do. Until then, just to repeat:<br /> <br /> Anarchs have Elders too :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T08:23:09-07:00","id":1524870,"title":"","content":"Who named this git? Were they aware they just took a half of Vampire and spelled it &quot;cool&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T11:55:11-07:00","id":1524875,"title":"","content":"There's also something a bit flat about the one moment where they show the dialogue-options. The NPC asks Phyre &quot;Who are you really?&quot; and the options are:<ul><li>Tell her everything</li> <li>Reveal your mark</li> <li>Assert your status</li> </ul>And the second one is chosen but Phyre's answer isn't just her showing the mark but explaining how she's been in hundred year long sleep from which she has been awoken. It doesn't feel like there's a huge difference between those three options. The third one strikes me as being the same as the first one except your character has a meaner tone. This style of dialogue-options really reminds me of those Bioware-games like Mass Effect and Dragon Age. You get the option to either be nice and honest, be neutral and an option to be mean. But it doesn't have this sprawling freedom you have like in Baldurs Gate 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T14:16:50-07:00","id":1524884,"title":"","content":"My impression was that the dialogue approach was meant to be similar to the Bioware style, but the NPC reactions are more branched. As noted, there aren't supposed to be Paragon and Renegade options. So picking being mean or being nice doesn't feed into a single meter of how you treat people. It sounds like what they want is for each significant NPC to have a few impression-scales they have about your character, so each reacts to you choices on their own metrics. I'd imagine this means they coded the NPCs more like how the more recent Civilization games do for individual leaders, where each leader has a few sliders and binary flags that dictate how much they like your civilization and thus what diplomatic options you get with them.<br /> <br /> Even if that specific preview snippet doesn't have a lot of nuance in the options (but then again we also only see one option, and we don't see any second or third order consequences), I think the intent is for something between ME and BG3. That actually does feel appropriate to me for a VtM game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T04:21:18-07:00","id":1524905,"title":"","content":"How does Bloodlines 1 have better facial animations than Bloodlines 2 ??? When an incomplete game from 2004 has better facial animations than your 2024 game? You should quit<br /> Just... quit and find a new job<br /> Pre-Alpha and Post-Alpha this &quot;vampire&quot; for some reason looks like my cat on his litterbox staring in to the distance while doing his thing... except this &quot;Pyre&quot; look like that <i>all the time</i><br /> By the way, I don't get it.. if B2 should be in the V5 setting, how on earth this could be a 100+ years old &quot;Elder&quot;? Well I guess Elder is a loose term... no to mention I couldn't help but noticed the lack of archaic in looks, mannerisms and speech (and name?).<br /> The Slayer from Cairo<br /> With a damn thin-blood, Fabien &quot;stuck&quot; in your head like in a reverse-diableire thing?<br /> Oy vey<br /> I think they - just like the W5 team - never even looked at the source material and just went &quot;Fuck it! Guys, whats popular at the moment in the industry? Okay, lets put that in. And make it a bit Mass Effect or Cyberpunk 2077-like! They were cool ,yes? And stamp a Bloodlines names on it, maybe no one will notice&quot;<br /> And, dear Set, this supposed to be the flagship rpg for VtM?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 11-02-2023, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T17:04:10-07:00","id":1524943,"title":"","content":"Chinese Room doesn't seem to understand what made Bloodlines so amazing, from a gameplay perspective.<br /> <br /> Maybe they'll actually tell a good VtM story, but that alone does not a Bloodlines sequel make...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj","name":"guiskj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2611_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T02:51:09-07:00","id":1524963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524870#post1524870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who named this git? Were they aware they just took a half of Vampire and spelled it &quot;cool&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That's the kind of name I would have thought was cool when I was 13. Maybe added an X to it, X-phyre. That name is really going to take me out of the story everything someone says it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T03:19:41-07:00","id":1524965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524870#post1524870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who named this git? Were they aware they just took a half of Vampire and spelled it &quot;cool&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524963#post1524963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. That's the kind of name I would have thought was cool when I was 13. Maybe added an X to it, X-phyre. That name is really going to take me out of the story everything someone says it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I have a PTSD-like flashbacks; it is like &quot;the Verse&quot; from Jupiter Ascending<br /> Universe wasn't cool enough, so the Wachowskis re-named it<br /> This is similar, just - if it possible - worse<br /> Just to be fun: The name Phyre is primarily a gender-neutral name of American origin that means <b>Fire</b>.\u200b<br /> Or Phyre is a Boy name, meaning &quot;<b>one who burns brightly</b>\u200b&quot; in Armenian origin.\u200b<br /> The Phyre family name was found in <i>Scotland</i> in 1901. In 1901 there was 1 Phyre family living in Lanarkshire.\u200b..<br /> In any case, it is probably just a &quot;nickname&quot; for the Slayer of Cairo<br /> The sad part?<br /> Cairo have a really rich history in WoD with S-tier Elders like the Cappadocian Angelique, direct Child of Lazarus, the Settiete Sleeping Lord, Child of The Scorpion King, the Banu Haqim Antara ibn Shaddad ibn Amr, also known as the Shepherd of Wolves<br /> Even the relativly young Gangrel, Nadima al-Muqanna, the Priestess of Dreams worth a mention (who are the leader of the Disciples of Anubis who are guided by the entity of the same name, who is so ancitent even the Ferrymen and Charon are indebted to him....)<br /> And we got... <br /> ...Phyre<br /> Let put all these aside<br /> My main problem is, so far what we saw, Bloodlines 2 only nominally a Bloodlines game, it lack the charm of the original<br /> Maybe the nostalgia talking... \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T03:41:01-07:00","id":1524967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524870#post1524870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who named this git? Were they aware they just took a half of Vampire and spelled it &quot;cool&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;My name's Phyre, Vam Phyre.&quot; You mean like that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T03:44:24-07:00","id":1524968,"title":"","content":"In her case it should be &quot;My name is Dred... Kin Dred&quot; since the term &quot;kindred&quot; in WoD came about in the 15th or 16th century, after the Great Anarch Revolt.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T04:56:33-07:00","id":1524969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524905#post1524905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a damn thin-blood, Fabien &quot;stuck&quot; in your head like in a reverse-diableire thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just assumed it was an actual diablere, with this not being Phyre\u200b's original body. The voice of Fabian is all that's left of the original thief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 11-03-2023, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T07:14:53-07:00","id":1524974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524967#post1524967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;My name's Phyre, Vam Phyre.&quot; You mean like that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524968#post1524968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In her case it should be &quot;My name is Dred... Kin Dred&quot; since the term &quot;kindred&quot; in WoD came about in the 15th or 16th century, after the Great Anarch Revolt.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it feels like something straight out of a Simspon's skit. &quot;I'm looking for a Vam. Vamphyre. Anyone seen a vamphyre around here?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T10:53:25-07:00","id":1524979,"title":"","content":"Or that Rick and Morty episode with Coach Feratu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T13:44:14-07:00","id":1524987,"title":"","content":"I'm really confused by what I have seen from this game. The trailers seemed to be really brutally focussed on first person perspective combat. The previews we have seen of the conversation choices seem quite limiting. I understand that not every RPG can have options as great as Baldurs Gate 3. But this seems to completely miss why people loved the first bloodlines game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7279-ichneumon","name":"Ichneumon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7279_6.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T14:37:47-07:00","id":1524992,"title":"","content":"One design-choice I don't like is how it was mentioned that your clothes will have an impact on the game. But as we have seen before, players will spend most of the game in first person so really, who cares about the clothes...? It's a similar issue I had with Cyberpunk 2077 where you have this huge wardrobe of clothes and then most of the time you're stuck in first person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T16:50:45-07:00","id":1524999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524992#post1524992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One design-choice I don't like is how it was mentioned that your clothes will have an impact on the game. But as we have seen before, players will spend most of the game in first person so really, who cares about the clothes...? It's a similar issue I had with Cyberpunk 2077 where you have this huge wardrobe of clothes and then most of the time you're stuck in first person.</div> </div> </div> </div>CP at least has an elaborate photo mode that's quite worth the while dressing up, and I spent way too much time dressing up my paperdoll.<br /> <br /> However, I would like to point out that most of the time in Bloodlines you were in some very, very shitty combat. Timewise more of your game was spent with the tiring necessary dungeons than it was in conversations or in cool moody places like the Hotel. But we don't remember the Bloodlines for that, we remember it for the story, the characters, for the impact your disciplines had on the social elements, for the emulation of the game and the experience of being a Malkavian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T17:07:54-07:00","id":1525002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524992#post1524992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One design-choice I don't like is how it was mentioned that your clothes will have an impact on the game. But as we have seen before, players will spend most of the game in first person so really, who cares about the clothes...? It's a similar issue I had with Cyberpunk 2077 where you have this huge wardrobe of clothes and then most of the time you're stuck in first person.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the sounds of it, the clothes you're wearing will impact how NPCs react to you and in turn impact the dialogue options available to you. Like a Prince is going to take you a lot more seriously dressed in a well-tailored suit than they would if you're dressed like some punk rock reject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T17:48:27-07:00","id":1525004,"title":"","content":"Here's some food for thought: When we got the first previews a couple of months ago, there was no talk of &quot;Oh, this is just post-alpha and maybe this will change.&quot;. So, where's that sudden caution coming from? How far into development is this game actually? Hopefully, this isn't one of those development-cycles where everything's bet on crunch making it all work... You know, doing the whole &quot;Bioware-magic&quot;-thing (since they've mentioned Mass Effect so often).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1525002#post1525002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From the sounds of it, the clothes you're wearing will impact how NPCs react to you and in turn impact the dialogue options available to you. Like a Prince is going to take you a lot more seriously dressed in a well-tailored suit than they would if you're dressed like some punk rock reject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, clothes have a mechanical impact on you character in Cyberpunk 2077, too. It's about seeing the character you dressed up on your screen. With a first person perspective you don't get that. <br /> <br /> It's not like third person perspective is inherently better than first person. Rather it's that if you present the option of dressing up a player-character (especially if game-mechanics push you to care about it), a third person perspective is more rewarding than a first-person-one, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T18:24:37-07:00","id":1525007,"title":"","content":"Considering how unpolished things look, I don't really see this releasing in 2024.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T21:05:52-07:00","id":1525010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524992#post1524992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One design-choice I don't like is how it was mentioned that your clothes will have an impact on the game. But as we have seen before, players will spend most of the game in first person so really, who cares about the clothes...? It's a similar issue I had with Cyberpunk 2077 where you have this huge wardrobe of clothes and then most of the time you're stuck in first person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that combat is First Person, but dialogue appears to be Third Person. So you'll see your character's clothing and whatnot when you go into the dialogue screen. So it should be a bit less of an issue than Cyberpunk 2077 was, since in that game even when you were engaging in dialogue with people, it was still in First Person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T00:10:17-07:00","id":1525013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524992#post1524992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One design-choice I don't like is how it was mentioned that your clothes will have an impact on the game. But as we have seen before, players will spend most of the game in first person so really, who cares about the clothes...? It's a similar issue I had with Cyberpunk 2077 where you have this huge wardrobe of clothes and then most of the time you're stuck in first person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right? The reason in the Souls franchise the word &quot;fashion souls&quot; is even a concept is that it's a 3rd person series. You spend A LOT of your time looking at your character running around. So players love to dress their character up in cool outfits, like the digital dollies they are. Going to great lengths against impossible odds, not for wealth or to save a dying world, but for THE DRIP.<br /> <br /> Fashion is a lot less important when you spend most of your time looking through the character's eyes. You might as well have a static character portrait, as in CRPGs of old, for all the difference it makes to the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T05:27:53-07:00","id":1525020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1525010#post1525010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worth noting that combat is First Person, but dialogue appears to be Third Person. So you'll see your character's clothing and whatnot when you go into the dialogue screen. So it should be a bit less of an issue than Cyberpunk 2077 was, since in that game even when you were engaging in dialogue with people, it was still in First Person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe... I could also see it doing the third-person-perspective only in important scenes. But I guess we'll see.<br /> <br /> With Cyberpunk 2077 I think it helps that you have Johnny Silverhand as an actual character standing in your field of vision so it isn't just the person you're talking to that you see. That mixes it up a bit. Of course, it's more work-intensive but I think that works better than just zooming in on Phyre's face whenever Fabian talks. Hopefully, they can come up with a better visual indicator til the game's release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T14:43:27-07:00","id":1525032,"title":"","content":"Is this a Double A game not a Triple A game.<br /> <br /> So there's not a Triple A set of graphics and good, I think every game like that is trash these days, Too much focus on graphics. They should keep things more stylized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T15:13:25-07:00","id":1525034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1525032#post1525032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a Double A game not a Triple A game.<br /> <br /> So there's not a Triple A set of graphics and good, I think every game like that is trash these days, Too much focus on graphics. They should keep things more stylized.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be unrealistic to expect Paradox to aim for anything similar to what you'd get from studios like Ubisoft or Activision/Blizzard (although from what I hear of the newest COD-release, I guess, quality-control isn't much of a priority over there these days). So I don't think one should expect the WOD-license to end up producing a ton of triple-A-games.<br /> <br /> BUT...! There's one exception to this: Bloodlines 2. That's supposed to be the tentpole. The sequel to a beloved cult-classic. Already the fact that it was that game which ended up in development-hell was bad. Now the pressure on it being remarkable has only grown stronger.<br /> <br /> When the trailers for the Chinese-Room-version first came out a couple of months ago, I lamented the lack of more extensive gameplay-videos. But with the latest video talking about &quot;post-alpha footage&quot;, I was a bit surprised. I assumed they would already be further along in the development. Now we don't really know when that handover to Chinese Room actually happened which I feel is a mistake. Just how long have they actually been working on this game? Hopefully, the release-date of Fall 2024 is something Chinese Room thinks it can make work rather than Paradox just wanting that to be the release-date. Cases like Redfall, Cyberpunk 2077 or that absolute travesty that was the Gollum-game have shown what happens when games are pushed out the door because investors/publishers insist on a particular release-date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T02:24:57-08:00","id":1525058,"title":"","content":"AA and AAA are also meaningless industry jargon at this point. Remember when they started to try to hype up AAAA games as a thing?<br /> <br /> Corporate overlords are demanding inane profit growth and don't care if it comes from worse games, scummy microtransactions, or screwing employees, so the teams capable of making A+ games are hamstrung from doing so, while smaller developers have better and better tools to make games that can compete with the big name companies.<br /> <br /> This is the best time for a small studio (though TCR has a lot of partners in BL2 that have much deeper pockets) to go after big studios and their &quot;AAA&quot; games. We keep seeing customers flocking to games from smaller studios because the games are good and for at least some time free from executive meddling (until they eventually can't afford to say know to being bought for giant piles of money). There's more than just making the game fun to play (timing, market saturation for that type of game, etc.) but you have to embrace what you're doing. Good retro games know what's beloved about old games, and what they need to do to keep modern gamers happy at the same time. Games that embrace what their core experience really is are going to do better than games that try to make a $100 million game for $50 million, instead of making a great $50 million project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T04:42:33-08:00","id":1525066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1525058#post1525058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AA and AAA are also meaningless industry jargon at this point. Remember when they started to try to hype up AAAA games as a thing?<br /> <br /> Corporate overlords are demanding inane profit growth and don't care if it comes from worse games, scummy microtransactions, or screwing employees, so the teams capable of making A+ games are hamstrung from doing so, while smaller developers have better and better tools to make games that can compete with the big name companies.<br /> <br /> This is the best time for a small studio (though TCR has a lot of partners in BL2 that have much deeper pockets) to go after big studios and their &quot;AAA&quot; games. We keep seeing customers flocking to games from smaller studios because the games are good and for at least some time free from executive meddling (until they eventually can't afford to say know to being bought for giant piles of money). There's more than just making the game fun to play (timing, market saturation for that type of game, etc.) but you have to embrace what you're doing. Good retro games know what's beloved about old games, and what they need to do to keep modern gamers happy at the same time. Games that embrace what their core experience really is are going to do better than games that try to make a $100 million game for $50 million, instead of making a great $50 million project.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agree. But try telling the corporate overlords that... And this year alone <a href=\"https://www.gamesindustry.biz/over-6000-games-industry-jobs-lost-in-2023-so-far\" target=\"_blank\">over 6000 game-developers have lost their job</a>. Because a game doing &quot;okay&quot; is not good enough and then immediately leads to people getting fired. And that reminds me of that whole discourse surrounding Baldurs Gate 3 when some developers were like &quot;Please don't expect other RPG-games to be on the same level as Baldurs Gate 3&quot;. And while Baldurs Gate 3's development by Larian Studios is atypical, that says more about the general state of the industry than Larian, I think. None of these other companies could ever produce something like Baldurs Gate 3 when these studios fire tons of their employees at the first sign of trouble. When these companies do that, either expertise or opportunities to build up that expertise get lost. Then add stuff like with Call of Duty where companies are pushing developers hard to push annual releases. And so the quality of these games suffers.<br /> <br /> But of course, for those corporate overlords the only metric that matters is infinite growth and with the economy not doing so well the area where they want to cut costs is employees...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T14:56:53-08:00","id":1525088,"title":"","content":"Double A games can be great, just look at ROBOCOP: ROGUE CITY.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T14:58:21-08:00","id":1525089,"title":"","content":"Those numbers don't even include companies trying to hide crunch-time by hiring lots of freelancers to work on individual pieces of a project, and then not giving them new contracts or even extending contracts so new freelancers have to pick up stuff other people designed. The idea of replacing burning out your programmers and developers with a lot of temporary freelancers isn't inherently bad, but it's been tainted into horror when contract manipulation to keep up that growth overrides any logic of workflow management.<br /> <br /> And consider if you look at that link, Microsoft is notorious for forcing their subsidiary game studios into this practice So when you look at the layoffs under Microsoft's watch, that's after Microsoft has earned a reputation for games that are terrible at launch and need two to four years of work before they're actually where they should have been at start due to freelancer-crunch-manipulations of people that were never going to have a job for more than a few months or count as getting laid off when their contract ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T01:00:26-08:00","id":1525108,"title":"","content":"We also see employees in the games industry laid off <i>even if the game they worked on did really well</i>. Even if the publisher is making record profits.<br /> <br /> Because to these businesses, making more money than ever is the right time to fire all their staff and hire new people at a fraction of the pay, to consolidate those gains.<br /> <br /> Doesn't matter if this gets rid of the very people who made that profit possible. It doesn't matter if it means losing hard-won institutional knowledge, and forces developers to train new employees from scratch. It doesn't matter that the games they just made are now harder to maintain in the future, because the people who knew how it worked were just fired.<br /> <br /> If they aren't making the most amount of money in that moment, the corporations could not care less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T02:58:40-08:00","id":1525111,"title":"","content":"We see that with Bungie and Destiny 2 right now. The game was struggling a bit and so what was the management's big idea for dealing with that in the latest expansion...? <a href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/paultassi/2023/02/17/destiny-2-makes-a-mistake-with-a-new-lightfall-microtransaction/\" target=\"_blank\">Adding <i>more</i> monetization</a>. Because that was the priority: How can Destiny 2 wring even more money out of the playerbase? And that decision led to things getting even worse, of course. And what was the next move after that...? <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-10-31/sony-s-bungie-game-unit-cut-jobs-as-destiny-2-popularity-waned\" target=\"_blank\">Mass-layoffs</a>.<br /> <br /> And you already have a little bit of that in Bloodlines 2 here by making 2 Clans DLC. If it's day-1-DLC then they actually already finished development and it shouldn't be cut out of the game just so that they can sell it to you separately. If it's DLC that gets released later on, it would've been better to just keep the development going until the game could be released with 6 Clans rather than 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T13:42:55-08:00","id":1525132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524870#post1524870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who named this git? Were they aware they just took a half of Vampire and spelled it &quot;cool&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone mixed up the flavors of 90's nostalgia perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T15:31:19-08:00","id":1525134,"title":"","content":"Hi I'm not a walking masqerade breach to happen with a blatant name to tip you off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-06-2023, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T13:07:53-08:00","id":1525177,"title":"","content":"The first playable Clan has been revealed: It's the <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/clans/brujah\" target=\"_blank\">Brujah</a>! (Well, not a huge surprise they are one of the four playable ones...)<br /> <br /> It isn't a big reveal in terms of content. You got a 16 second video and the announcement that we will get more info in early 2024 on what all the Brujah powers look like. In the video, you see your typical action-game charge-ability which is... not impressive. It fits the Clan but gameplay-wise it's something we've seen in many games before.<br /> <br /> Also, it's notable that this preview-page features barely any lore on the Clan and while it is mentioned that the vampiric powers are called Disciplines the text proceeds to talk in very game-y terms about it rather than referencing the classic Discipline-spread of the Brujah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T01:54:37-08:00","id":1525196,"title":"","content":"I keep feeling that with everything I see of this game, it feels like a generic modern video game, and not an attempt at creating a video game version of what it is like to play Vampire: The Masquerade. It feels utterly boring to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7279-ichneumon","name":"Ichneumon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7279_6.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T03:39:43-08:00","id":1525201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524965#post1524965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, it is probably just a &quot;nickname&quot; for the Slayer of Cairo</div> </div> </div> </div>What is that &quot;Slayer of Cairo&quot; thing about anyway? My knowledge about Bloodlines 2 borders on nill at the moment....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1524965#post1524965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sad part?<br /> Cairo have a really rich history in WoD with S-tier Elders like the Cappadocian Angelique, direct Child of Lazarus, the Settiete Sleeping Lord, Child of The Scorpion King, the Banu Haqim Antara ibn Shaddad ibn Amr, also known as the Shepherd of Wolves<br /> Even the relatively young Gangrel, Nadima al-Muqanna, the Priestess of Dreams worth a mention (who are the leader of the Disciples of Anubis who are guided by the entity of the same name, who is so ancitent even the Ferrymen and Charon are indebted to him....)<br /> And we got...<br /> ...Phyre</div> </div> </div> </div>More like Meths galore you mean, since Nadima is the only one amidst the NPCs you cited who's less than 1400+ years old. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (As an aside, it always mildly annoyed me how Angelique &amp; Kahina both seem to play like variants of the same template, at least IMHO. Would like to see other people's thoughts on those two or other elements of the city's kindred history)\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ichneumon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1525196#post1525196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep feeling that with everything I see of this game, it feels like a generic modern video game, and not an attempt at creating a video game version of what it is like to play Vampire: The Masquerade. It feels utterly boring to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be wholy fair, the original Vampire: Bloodlines didn't start as the cult classic it became - it took the active de-bugging and modding by a quite active community of Vampire: The Masquerade fans for it to get there. So, maybe not the start we wished for, but not quite as terrible as could be, all things considered?<br /> <br /> Guess what we make out of Bloodlines or any spin-off/sequel as such is what really interests me.<br /> <br /> Has anyone toyed with their own tabletop version of the events in the game like the chapter in BJD or spin-offs like the LA By Night web series?<br /> Kind of curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-05-2024, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T11:41:43-08:00","id":1525214,"title":"","content":"And the amazing PR and marketing continues as they announce the Brujah as the first clan available. You know the same thing that was announced over a year ago. And we'll get to know more about the Brujah in January with a more indepth review.<br /> <br /> So we get a reveal that more will be revealed in January about something that was already revealed.<br /> <br /> A+ marketing. My enthusiasim is as high as their skill at marketing.<br /> <br /> Can someone please just buy the IP from Paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T12:11:19-08:00","id":1525215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1525201#post1525201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is that &quot;Slayer of Cairo&quot; thing about anyway? My knowledge about Bloodlines 2 borders on nill at the moment....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In the linked video in 12:42 that Nosferatu (?) Willem called her that<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1525214#post1525214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You know the same thing that was announced over a year ago. And we'll get to know more about the Brujah in January with a more indepth review.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that almost two minute announcement was miles better and actually showed <i>what</i> a Brujah <i>is</i><br /> I don't like the Brujah that much, but that intro? I'm not ashamed to admit it had me hyped!<br /> Now this 15 sec (less actually) managed only to dissapoint<br /> It really showed us what a Brujah is, how and why they are the &quot;The Learned Clan, Rabble, Punks, Hipsters, Prometheans, Rebels, Philosopher-Kings, Hellenes.&quot; and by their won words: &quot;Brujah is the learned clan, the clan of radicals, the clan commonly misjudged as punks looking for trouble, the Brujah are guided by passion and dedication to an ideal.&quot;<br /> Yes sir!<br /> That not even 15 sec totally showed us!<br /> Sorry, bile coming up, where is the puke bucket....?\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T15:07:17-08:00","id":1525221,"title":"","content":"I can just picture the Ventrue or Lasombra looking at the Brujah and thinking &quot;If they ever get their act together and be organized, then we might be worried about them being a true danger to us.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T22:18:21-08:00","id":1525232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1525215#post1525215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the linked video in 12:42 that Nosferatu (?) Willem called her that</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, random title drop with zero buildup, such great word-smithing (not)....<br /> <br /> To be honest Willem seemed and sounded a damn lot more interesting Her blandness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T22:58:12-08:00","id":1525233,"title":"","content":"Yes<br /> World-building at it best, amirite?<br /> And that &quot;title&quot; should be meaningfull, the past with Cairo an important part/lore of your story - at least judging by the way Willem acted, its affected his behaviour and attitude not to mention expectations regarding Phyre<br /> Yet we know nothing<br /> Oaky this could change, but frankly, I highly doubt and everyone and their grandma' in Game will know way more than us about our own character - my two cents is, they will play the amnesia card to make it &quot;easy&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T23:23:50-08:00","id":1525235,"title":"","content":"While we'll have to see about actual execution, the previews so far have stated they're not doing the amnesia approach. From the sound of it the game will have a mix of Bioware style broad strokes background selections where you pick a handful of things about your character that will offer unique options in certain dialogue trees, as well as retroactive story bits where dialogues will bring up stories about Phyre, and the player can select if a story is true, false, or something in the middle; while also letting you select dialogue to use the stories to lie and manipulate NPCs.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is a bad idea. Letting the player write their character's story as they go is a good way to handle this without needing to be lazy via amnesia, or dump hours lots of non-interactive exposition on the player<br /> <br /> Like combat though, we still are being told what's going to be in the game, without any of these game play videos actually showing enough to say that it's there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T03:14:34-08:00","id":1525241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1525235#post1525235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we'll have to see about actual execution, the previews so far have stated they're not doing the amnesia approach. From the sound of it the game will have a mix of Bioware style broad strokes background selections where you pick a handful of things about your character that will offer unique options in certain dialogue trees, as well as retroactive story bits where dialogues will bring up stories about Phyre, and the player can select if a story is true, false, or something in the middle; while also letting you select dialogue to use the stories to lie and manipulate NPCs.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is a bad idea. Letting the player write their character's story as they go is a good way to handle this without needing to be lazy via amnesia, or dump hours lots of non-interactive exposition on the player<br /> <br /> Like combat though, we still are being told what's going to be in the game, without any of these game play videos actually showing enough to say that it's there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Background exposition &amp; customization through character dialogue is a valid tool - my current chronicle has seen the players getting a lot of milleage out of that in and out of Elysium, to be fair.<br /> <br /> The somewhat lackluster sample of execution we get in the cutscene (ok, not quite a cutscene if there are choices but you get what i mean) is what bothers me. But yeah, probably too little and too soon to fairly judge the game's actual merits or lack thereof. The original Bloodlines itself had a pretty bumpy run back then. Time will tell.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T04:16:52-08:00","id":1525242,"title":"","content":"For a game that's supposed to come out in a year, I feel like they are showing way too little gameplay. Like with the Slayer-stuff and interacting with that. It could just be something like in one scene Phyre says &quot;Yes, I'm the Slayer of Cairo.&quot; and then we could've been shown another scene where one of the dialogue-options is something like &quot; (Slayer of Cairo) You don't want to cross me, believe me.&quot;. That sort of basic &quot;backgrounds unlock dialogue-options&quot;-stuff. Instead what we got in that story &amp; narrative video was way more basic than that. And the rest was all tell and no show.<br /> <br /> Also, to now find out that the Clan-reveals have been drawn out as a preview yet again with the full reveals happening in early 2024... what a disappointment. Revealing four Clan-names plus 15-second videos of one power available to each Clan doesn't make for a great preview.<br /> <br /> And in a way, it still is unclear what the game is about. I mean, we got the &quot;Thin-Blood in your head plus mysterious ritual that awakened an Elder&quot;-bit but that's more plot than story. And hopefully, there's more going on in the game than the main-character running around and asking people who did that to them and why. It's a bit of a whodunnit-mystery, sure, but why should anybody care about that? So I don't think they have done a good job either in getting anyone invested in the actual story of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-14T11:34:35-08:00","id":1525430,"title":"","content":"The next playable Clan has been revealed: <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/clans/tremere\" target=\"_blank\">Tremere</a>. Same as with the Brujah, we got a 15-second-video of gameplay. The other interesting thing mentioned is that during the course of the game you will be able to unlock all costumes for Phyre.<br /> <br /> But I think I need to make a note about the video here. First, there's more going on in it than in the video last week with the Brujah-character. There are good and bad news, though. The good news is that we didn't just see one ability in this (very short) video. It starts with an ability to pull an opponent off a ledge via an unseen force, then the character punches an opponent in front of them and the impact not just affects the punched opponent but the one standing behind them as well and both are thrown back quite forcefully. Then we get to see the Tremere-specific ability that you charge up and in the course of that &quot;missiles&quot; are summoned that you then let loose upon the enemy.<br /> <br /> Well, here's the bad news: Having looked at the video slowed down, there are some significant cuts in there and you can see why. The first one is that when the opponent is pulled from the ledge before he lands, there's a hard cut. Then after punching the one opponent that ends in two opponents being thrown back, I'm pretty sure you can see the the second opponent who stood behind the first one bugging out (he levitates in the air, probably got caught in the environment-physics somehow). That's when the second hard cut happens. Also when the missiles kill one of the opponents around 0 : 10, the ragdoll-physics on the opponent look rough. It literally looks like a doll whose strings got cut.<br /> <br /> It's supposed to come out in a year but honestly, it looks rough. There's a lot of work ahead for Chinese Room to make this presentable. But at least, it's now clear why you can't just show 15 minutes of uninterrupted gameplay or something like that.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T05:51:03-08:00","id":1526226,"title":"","content":"So. Banu Haqim. Who saw that coming? I never thought the Cairo reference could have any substance to the clan choices. It does feel like the game will be VERY fighty. And if that was Quietus, I am a bit dissapointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T06:46:11-08:00","id":1526227,"title":"","content":"Out of place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","user":"Psicose","date":". 12-02-2023, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T06:51:26-08:00","id":1526229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1526226#post1526226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Banu Haqim. Who saw that coming? I never thought the Cairo reference could have any substance to the clan choices. It does feel like the game will be VERY fighty. And if that was Quietus, I am a bit dissapointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where that was quietus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T07:05:47-08:00","id":1526230,"title":"","content":"Banu Haquim... Hmm, wouldn't have expected that. But there seems to be quite the focus on how they could slot into combat-play with these Clan-choices (Brujah: Strength and close combat, Tremere: Blood Sorcery as a weapon to be used from the distance and Banu Haquim: focus on stealth). But like usual the 15-second bit of &quot;gameplay&quot; looks to be in the <i>very early</i> stages of development.<br /> <br /> The preview also included a scene we've seen last month and it seems they had the voice-actor for Phyre re-record her lines in that scene to give more of a threatening tone to the line-reading and accompanying that they also re-animated the expressions of Phyre. It looks and sounds better but is the idea here that they're going to re-do all the Phyre-stuff both in terms of voice-acting and animation...?<br /> <br /> The developers also talked about &quot;Phyre &amp; Narrative&quot; in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O6TJO1WlvDU\" target=\"_blank\">this video</a>. But my big thing with video-games these days is &quot;Unless you show me the gameplay, I don't believe you.&quot;. And even there we had already incidents where previewed gameplay-footage turned out to be fake once the actual game got released.<br /> <br /> Also, it's really weird that they haven't shown off the male voice for Phyre. In the video linked above they are constantly referring to Phyre as &quot;she&quot; and in the comments the WOD-Youtube-Account explained: &quot;We have only shown female model for Phyre so far, so it's just easier for developers to refer to her this way. Worry not - male model will be shown in the future! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot;. Why does the male model and male voice-actor for Phyre need to be this extra reveal that happens in the future...? There's nothing groundbreaking about having a male and a female version of an RPG-videogame-protagonist.<br /> <br /> I just gotta say: The only thing these previews have done so far is succeed in giving me some serious doubts this game will be ready for release in Q4 2024.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T08:08:21-08:00","id":1526231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1526226#post1526226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> if that was Quietus, I am a bit dissapointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>In V5 no such thing exist anyway, Banu Haqim have Blood Sorcery, Celerity, Obfuscate<br /> And they cling to V5 like no tomorrow, so I highly doubt we will see any &quot;pre-V5&quot; disciplines \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T09:47:04-08:00","id":1526233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1526231#post1526231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In V5 no such thing exist anyway, Banu Haqim have Blood Sorcery, Celerity, Obfuscate<br /> And they cling to V5 like no tomorrow, so I highly doubt we will see any &quot;pre-V5&quot; disciplines \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>They could simply give Banu Haqim and Tremere two seperate disciplines that share only the name to maintain the V5 &quot;party line&quot;. I don't think the kind of powers the Tremere will get out of blood sorcery would fit the intended playstyle of Banu Haqim's stealth or vice versa in Tremere's magic/ranged (I'm assuming they're pushing these specific playstyles based on 15 seconds of footage, so I maybe wrong!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28009-macja","name":"macja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T14:51:36-08:00","id":1526253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1526230#post1526230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just gotta say: The only thing these previews have done so far is succeed in giving me some serious doubts this game will be ready for release in Q4 2024.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, based on what they've shown and what they are intentionally not showing, I don't believe there is any chance this game comes out next year, unless it's either incredibly short or a complete buggy mess. It's looking like it's mid-2025 at the soonest. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T16:57:58-08:00","id":1526258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1526229#post1526229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where that was quietus?</div> </div> </div> </div>I got no idea what it was. There was strange blood stuff and time stopping and ragdolling people.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1526231#post1526231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In V5 no such thing exist anyway, Banu Haqim have Blood Sorcery, Celerity, Obfuscate<br /> And they cling to V5 like no tomorrow, so I highly doubt we will see any &quot;pre-V5&quot; disciplines \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Quietus got ported into Blood Sorcery?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T18:04:13-08:00","id":1526260,"title":"","content":"I can't believe they're using the &quot;Saracen&quot; sobriquet for the Banu Haqim on the game page. I guess they're now officially the Arab/Muslim clan and we've forgotten the context of the Crusades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T19:19:26-08:00","id":1526261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1526258#post1526258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got no idea what it was. There was strange blood stuff and time stopping and ragdolling people.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I thought Quietus got ported into Blood Sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>It looked like Celerity, Obfuscate and Potence, although the latter seems unlikely. Nothing in the video looked like any of Blood Sorcery's more Haqimite powers like Scorpion's Touch or Baal's Caress, but how TCR interprets the discipline for the clan remains to be seen. If Hardsuit could make one of their two Malkavian disciplines Dementation, Troika could make Animalism the power to summon ephemeral animals out of nowhere and Jason Carl could homebrew instant fireball Lure of Flames in the show that was effectively V5's face on Twitch and Youtube, then I doubt that TCR are obligated to follow the rules <i>that</i> closely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T14:57:15-08:00","id":1526299,"title":"","content":"Another thing I've been wondering about... With Banu Haquim being an option and this whole &quot;Slayer of Cairo&quot;-thing that was mentioned, I gotta wonder: Are they truly gonna write stuff into the game that will make us believe Phyre is somebody from the turn of the 20th century in Egypt? Will they delve into the real-world-history of Egypt or will the game just pretend the Vampire-stuff is just happening in this &quot;parallel dimension&quot; so-to-speak where real-world-history is irrelevant? I mean, since the protagonist is an Elder there should be a historical dimension to the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T20:00:24-08:00","id":1526309,"title":"","content":"Correct if I'm wrong. We were supposed to see past the atrocity that was V5 because Paradox is a game company, so they're creating the bee's knees in terms of game with Bloodlines 2 using V5 system. Methinks this particular bee is legless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T15:10:53-08:00","id":1526332,"title":"","content":"I mean Bloodlines 2 was always going to be using V5 because that's the Edition Paradox is backing. Every recent VtM game has been V5 and Bloodlines 2 is pretty much in Paradox's eyes, the crown jewel of that which also why Paradox was never going to let Bloodlines 2 die as long as they were keen to keep owning WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T15:34:21-08:00","id":1526376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1526332#post1526332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean Bloodlines 2 was always going to be using V5 because that's the Edition Paradox is backing. Every recent VtM game has been V5 and Bloodlines 2 is pretty much in Paradox's eyes, the crown jewel of that which also why Paradox was never going to let Bloodlines 2 die as long as they were keen to keep owning WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, that was not the case of the original iteration of bloodlines 2. <br /> It's mostly seen in disciplines. Malkavian had access to dementation, which doesn't exist V5. Same for the two starting disciplines as a thin blood, which are legacy disciplines of caitif.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T18:27:51-08:00","id":1526383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1526332#post1526332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean Bloodlines 2 was always going to be using V5 because that's the Edition Paradox is backing. Every recent VtM game has been V5 and Bloodlines 2 is pretty much in Paradox's eyes, the crown jewel of that which also why Paradox was never going to let Bloodlines 2 die as long as they were keen to keep owning WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given development limbo has gotten so bad that the publicly stated protagonist, story, mechanics, and design direction of the game have been redone at least 3 times now, Paradox is likely going to be in for a rude awakening when they find out their crown jewel is an unconvincing, plastic replica of a more impressive gem.<br /> <br /> There's nothing to really say anymore. The writing was on the wall for a while now, most prominently back when WtO20 was controversially nerfed to what would later be recognized as the current street-level-only paradigm. I'd also say we're well into feeling the effects. Even as late as when the 20's were still the hot thing, every category could get thread responses any day of the week. Currently even the vtm threads can go multiple days with no activity. The fanbase is aging and there isn't enough influx of new people to replace the ones slowly giving up or moving on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T08:22:59-08:00","id":1526402,"title":"","content":"Okay, I said it before and the last Clan-reveal just confirms this: There's <i>no way</i> that this game is in a state where it comes out in a year. The only way it could is if it's either very buggy/unfinished or incredibly short.<br /> <br /> The fourth Clan has been revealed and it's... Ventrue. And here's what it says: &quot;Today, we\u2019d like to share the fourth clan with you: Ventrue. The clan assets for Ventrue are in the process of being finalized, and we will share assets and gameplay showing off the playstyle of Ventrue during next year.&quot; You thought a 15-second-video was too short - how about <i>zero</i> seconds...? Yeah, just great PR as usual...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T08:37:31-08:00","id":1526403,"title":"","content":"If there are no Gangrel, then I have no interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T14:18:06-08:00","id":1526421,"title":"","content":"The first four (though who thought having two more for later was a good idea is still beyond me) is an odd mix. What comes to mind:<br /> <br /> 1) Animalism, Protean,and Oblivion are the only V5 Disciplines not covered by the current options. I can almost see a justification here as these aren't the easiest to translate into a video game; esp. if you're not investing a lot of development in areas of play where they tend to shine in TTRPG use. BL1's versions of Animalism and Protean were pretty big departures from the TTRPG versions so they'd have something to do. Oblivion is a lot of work for effects that could be hard to make unique in the kind of game-play we're being given impressions of so far. That said, if they were avoiding these three Disciplines (or at least for now) they're cutting out a lot of classic VtM stuff for players to use first hand.<br /> <br /> 2) Speaking of, that only actually leaves three options for Clans left: Malkavian, Toreador, and Salubri. If the first point is remotely an issue for the game, I would predict Toreador and Salubri. Malkavian play would be less impactful when you already have a &quot;voice in your head&quot; character to deal with, and Salubri would let you bring the very different playstyle that the Nosferatu had in BL 1 of being visually Masquerade breaking, without having to worry about Animalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T15:04:38-08:00","id":1526424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1526421#post1526421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animalism, Protean,and Oblivion are the only V5 Disciplines not covered by the current options. I can almost see a justification here as these aren't the easiest to translate into a video game</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as far as Vampire Redemption we had some of Animalism and Protean. But how will the skill tree develop? Obviously Lasombras and some of the more exotic clans won't be even considered, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T17:28:59-08:00","id":1526427,"title":"","content":"Animalism and Protean in Redemption weren't exactly top tier Disciplines to get. Animalism was basically only worth it for Beckoning and getting an additional combat minion (though since what you can summon was based on Clan, the value was variable). Protean was more useful, but still suffered at lot since there very little benefit beyond Feral Claws.<br /> <br /> Redemption being much more of an old school cRPG combat-fest highlights the problem even if it had different priorities: a video game with specific focuses on what the character's can do drastically alters the value of some Disciplines when you remove the creativity and freedom you have in a TTRPG style game. Animalism isn't really useful if animals aren't part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T15:25:07-08:00","id":1526479,"title":"","content":"The lack of Malkvians as a playable clan is a bit worrisome and I've seen quite a bit of people disappointed with that. Malkavian was the most unique playthru in the original Bloodlines, and probably the one people remember the most. It was something a lot of people were looking forward to and ended up being a pretty major draw. Not having them at all (or arguably worse) having them as a day one DLC cashgrab that you have to pay extra for, is just going to leave Bloodlines fans feeling salty and less likely to purchase the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T16:38:24-08:00","id":1526483,"title":"","content":"With the &quot;voice of a thin-blood stuck in your head&quot; thing for helping to handle exposition, I think fans of the BL1 Malk play would be really disappointed with Malks in BL 2. Either they lose uniqueness because it's basically the same but the Malk is less certain the voice isn't just something they made up, or they get overburdened by trying to have both said voice and other things that demonstrate madness in some fashion.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T17:04:57-08:00","id":1526484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1526483#post1526483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the &quot;voice of a thin-blood stuck in your head&quot; thing for helping to handle exposition, I think fans of the BL1 Malk play would be really disappointed with Malks in BL 2. Either they lose uniqueness because it's basically the same but the Malk is less certain the voice isn't just something they made up, or they get overburdened by trying to have both said voice and other things that demonstrate madness in some fashion.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There might be a good reason for it. I'm just seeing lots of people are disappointed, and there's even a few clickbait news articles about the lack of Malkavians already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T00:20:18-08:00","id":1526504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1526483#post1526483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the &quot;voice of a thin-blood stuck in your head&quot; thing for helping to handle exposition, I think fans of the BL1 Malk play would be really disappointed with Malks in BL 2. Either they lose uniqueness because it's basically the same but the Malk is less certain the voice isn't just something they made up, or they get overburdened by trying to have both said voice and other things that demonstrate madness in some fashion.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the presence of a voice in your head that is objectively real (because it appears in other playthroughs) makes having Malkavian-specific delusions/hallucinations very weird. And not in a good way.<br /> <br /> Like, how does it even work? Is the Thin Blood in your head also cognizant of the Malk PC's warped perceptions? Will there be lots of incidents of the Thin Blood acting as a minder for the PC, keeping them on task and yanking them out of fugue states? Is that even <i>desirable</i> for a Malkavian playthrough, since the big breaks from reality were a core part of what made BL1's Malk playthrough so fun? At least when you're alone and mad, there's lots of interesting ways to mess with the player that can't really be objectively refuted. The subjectivity is part of the draw, and what makes a Malk game unique.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess, though, I'd say if the game DID get a Malkavian option, the Thin Blood's dialogue would almost never reflect the change (because implementing such radical narrative differences would take lots of development time the game obviously doesn't have). The game would treat it as if it's a normal playthrough, aside from very specific moments. Which misses the point of having a Malk option in a Bloodlines game.<br /> <br /> Either that, or it'll be a DLC that is a very short, contained experienced. Simply to avoid having to remake the main campaign from scratch. Which ALSO would be missing the point of having a Malk option in a Bloodlines game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T00:52:33-08:00","id":1526509,"title":"","content":"They could have the insane Malkavian seeing strange information within the game itself, like nothing appearing on the status screen or buggy characters, or hallucinations of things appearing like messages written in blood on the wall, radio noise in the background, maybe even some kind of enemy that appears only in that altered state that only he sees. Dialogue choices that only appear when he's in this state would also work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T05:37:01-08:00","id":1529416,"title":"","content":"The next trailer will be revealed on January 31st.<br /> <br /> But before that I think <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/visceral-immersive-combat\" target=\"_blank\">the latest Dev-Diary</a> gives us a good insight into what kind of game Bloodlines 2 actually is.<br /> <br /> First, it mentions these three playstyles. The examples it chooses are a bit... wild but okay.<br /> <br /> The first is &quot;Strategic Stalker&quot; which mentions Dishonored and doing stealth-builds in Fallout or Elder Scrolls. The second part is an interesting choice because stealth sucks in Bethesda games and is tied to very rudimentary systems (stealth-damage, detection-reduction... stuff like that). Dishonored meanwhile is an actual stealth-game based on sandbox-maps where special powers are available to the player to take out guards in multiple ways, find multiple ways to traverse the map and there's a bit of an expanded stealth-system. But I guess the main-takeaway here is that the game has a stealth-system. We'll see whether it's closer to a Bethesda-game or Dishonored.<br /> <br /> The second is &quot;Action Brawler&quot; and the games that are mentioned are God of War, Shadow of Mordor and Elden Ring. Hmm, now those are three very different types of action-games... Who knows what type of combat-system it exactly is but of course the first issue is definitely that all three of these examples are third-person-perspective games while Bloddlines 2 isn't one. And then there's of course the question of just how many tools you get to use in combats like moves, powers and whatnot as well as how much there is to the parry/dodge-mechanic.<br /> <br /> The third type is about narrative and the only thing that this sentence kinda sticks out: &quot;We envision that a core of the Bloodlines 1 fans identify with this playstyle and also fans of TCR's titles to date (and a lot of the developers working on the game), so we\u2019re making sure the gameplay pillar doesn\u2019t add action at the detriment of these important players.&quot;<br /> <br /> But I think the most revealing bit comes at the very end:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, how do we go about achieving this? We focus on immersion over complexity: A streamlined control scheme with actions that are easy for all three playstyles to pick up and play. We then build depth on top of these to give longer-term mastery for the players that want it. For example, the defensive mechanic is a dash, allowing players to dodge incoming attacks or reposition. If dodge is used towards an enemy performing a melee attack, it becomes a counter, staggering the enemy - it is fine for players to never do this move, but for those that want a higher skill-ceiling, it is there. How we use abilities is also streamlined, to maintain immersion. Abilities are mapped to the face buttons (on gamepad), limiting the player to 4 available at one time. This is a small enough amount that a player can use them without breaking their flow, but also deep enough, through the different ways you can combine and use them that it keeps combat engaging and fun. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Immersion over complexity&quot;... Hmm... Also, this indicates there's an expectation that you're gonna use a controller to play this game.<br /> <br /> And later on, I thought that was a bit of a weird thing to put in there: &quot;As an Elder vampire, Phyre has become desensitised to violence, and we want the same to happen to the player...&quot; You... do?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T07:14:18-08:00","id":1529425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529416#post1529416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The next trailer will be revealed on January 31st.<br /> <br /> But before that I think <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/visceral-immersive-combat\" target=\"_blank\">the latest Dev-Diary</a> gives us a good insight into what kind of game Bloodlines 2 actually is.<br /> <br /> First, it mentions these three playstyles. The examples it chooses are a bit... wild but okay.<br /> <br /> The first is &quot;Strategic Stalker&quot; which mentions Dishonored and doing stealth-builds in Fallout or Elder Scrolls. The second part is an interesting choice because stealth sucks in Bethesda games and is tied to very rudimentary systems (stealth-damage, detection-reduction... stuff like that). Dishonored meanwhile is an actual stealth-game based on sandbox-maps where special powers are available to the player to take out guards in multiple ways, find multiple ways to traverse the map and there's a bit of an expanded stealth-system. But I guess the main-takeaway here is that the game has a stealth-system. We'll see whether it's closer to a Bethesda-game or Dishonored.<br /> <br /> The second is &quot;Action Brawler&quot; and the games that are mentioned are God of War, Shadow of Mordor and Elden Ring. Hmm, now those are three very different types of action-games... Who knows what type of combat-system it exactly is but of course the first issue is definitely that all three of these examples are third-person-perspective games while Bloddlines 2 isn't one. And then there's of course the question of just how many tools you get to use in combats like moves, powers and whatnot as well as how much there is to the parry/dodge-mechanic.<br /> <br /> The third type is about narrative and the only thing that this sentence kinda sticks out: &quot;We envision that a core of the Bloodlines 1 fans identify with this playstyle and also fans of TCR's titles to date (and a lot of the developers working on the game), so we\u2019re making sure the gameplay pillar doesn\u2019t add action at the detriment of these important players.&quot;<br /> <br /> But I think the most revealing bit comes at the very end:<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Immersion over complexity&quot;... Hmm... Also, this indicates there's an expectation that you're gonna use a controller to play this game.<br /> <br /> And later on, I thought that was a bit of a weird thing to put in there: &quot;As an Elder vampire, Phyre has become desensitised to violence, and we want the same to happen to the player...&quot; You... do?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, if it was just Vampire: Dishonored with a lot more conversation, that would do a lot more to sell me on the game than anything they've said so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T07:22:27-08:00","id":1529426,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;action brawler&quot; thing is bizarre, given that Bloodlines 2 is a first person game. You'd think they'd be pointing towards other first person games like Cyberpunk or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T13:59:41-08:00","id":1529463,"title":"","content":"It feels like they mixed up, &quot;games we played that influenced our design for these modes,&quot; with, &quot;games to reference that will actually communicate the final product too potential players.&quot;<br /> <br /> For example, on the third play style, they could have easily referenced the Modern Control changes in Street Fighter 6 (which were added to make it easier for casual play by vastly reducing the complexity of the controller scheme if you don't want to be a sweaty competitive) to set expectations of how combat can work for people that don't want to go super in-depth on fighting, but still have options for those that want a more invested experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-25-2024, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T03:33:12-08:00","id":1529497,"title":"","content":"I doubt they will do anything that fancy in terms of accessibility as Street Fighter 6 did. It's probably just about how the mechanic is one of those dodge-mechanics that can turn into a counter when you time it right but the difficulty isn't set up in a way where the game expects players to do that. For example, like when you have one of those Souls-like games with a stagger-meter and timed counters are the best way to fill the stagger-meter of the enemy and therefore the game expects players to get proficient in timed counters (like in Sekiro, for example).<br /> <br /> And I mean the descriptions are only superficial anyway because it isn't like you're dropped into the game and you can choose any of these playstyles. I imagine the Clan you choose has some impact on how well you can engage with these playstyles. I doubt you will get much out of the Brujah-powers-set in a stealth-playthrough, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T10:13:09-08:00","id":1529762,"title":"","content":"The <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HwhvfH-Ij8Q\" target=\"_blank\">gameplay-trailer</a> is out. It shows once again the Willhem-scene but now it's the full scene and not just the dialogue. What it certainly emphasizes is that what we've seen before was indeed pre-alpha-footage.<br /> <br /> The gameplay looks okay. And we've finally got to see the UI! But it doesn't look good that we're still returning to the same scene that has been shown as a &quot;reveal&quot; three times at this point.<br /> <br /> Some other comments:<ul><li>Considering this is the Chinese Room we're talking about and the illusion-stuff in that section and the main-villain being a Malkavian... I wonder just how often this game will turn into these types of walking-simulator-horror-games with simple puzzles and reliance on these visual effects where you go into a room and when you turn around the room changes, that sort of stuff.</li> <li>The animations don't look great in combat. Also, I wonder with movement-abilities like the dash, first-person-perspective always feels bad when you get swarmed by enemies. It doesn't seem that outside of powers you get anything more than light and heavy punch and if combat only happens in restricted small areas like in this preview I guess, it won't be that big of an issue.</li> <li>At least it doesn't seem like you can get interrupted when you do these Feeding-scenes because of the way the abilities and health work, it seems like you will be doing quite a few of those in each combat. Hopefully, there's some variety to the animations.</li> <li>The new dialogue shown off with Willem where he has a bomb strapped to him seems like a typical dialogue-tree-puzzle where you have to choose the right option a couple of times based on some social deduction and stuff you learn in the sequence before to convince Willem not to blow himself up.</li> <li>Phyre was described in the interview afterwards and there was again this talk of &quot;leaning into the legend, lying about it etc.&quot; but honestly the descriptions just reminded me of how Shepard and their backstory was treated in Mass Effect. It's this cipher of a character that while treated like someone who already is part of the world, the emphasis is far more on what the character is doing after the game has started. I guess we'll see when they talk about what they call &quot;social feeding&quot; and how complex the roleplaying gets. Otherwise, you really should just pick the options in the Willem-scene that convince him to not blow himself up.</li> </ul><br /> Overall, I feel better about the game now than before but I'm still not convinced it won't have some adverse effect on something in this game that this is supposed to come out in less than a year. In a certain way, we've been following the active development of this Willem-scene as the dialogue-scene gets better facial animations and gets integrated into an actual game-sequence. I know, game-development is cutting it really close these days (lengthy crunch periods, day-one patches, misleading trailers etc.) when it comes to release-dates, though. Hopefully, this won't be one of those games that is launched in a broken state and instead of working on the promised DLC, the Chinese Room studio first has to fix all the problems and issues with the game (because releasing the game was deemed more important than properly finishing development).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T12:40:34-08:00","id":1529764,"title":"","content":"I really liked this gameplay trailer. I may not like Phyre as a concept since I wanted to play a Thin Blood not an Elder but the graphics are majorly improved. I hope they include the characters from the original game, though, like Ellif and Mr. Damp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T13:25:56-08:00","id":1529768,"title":"","content":"I think the only thing people may not like is that this section didn't give off major RPG-vibes. It was essentially a linear section with some atmospherical walking-sections, some combat-arenas, a basic puzzle and then a dialogue-tree-challenge that decides whether Willem blows himself up or not.<br /> <br /> As someone who's a videogamer and plays a lot, there was nothing in that trailer that impressed me. That atmospheric walking-stuff and environmental storytelling-stuff... neat but I wished it would then lead to something more involved than that sound-puzzle they have there. I mean, Arkham Asylum came out in 2009. I get it, Detective Sense is a neat little thing but at this point I want to see something more interesting than running around a room chasing a sound. At least, they didn't make it worse by having enemies attack you. But it's still just boring busywork to repeatedly have to run around and press F on that grammophon. Just do a cutscene instead where the character relays his backstory instead of me having to move around that room chasing that music. There isn't even interesting environmental storytelling happening like changing the room to reflect parts of the story. But of course that stuff would require time to do that - which Chinese Room don't have.<br /> <br /> Combat similarly... not impressive. If light punch, heavy punch, dodge and feed is all I'm doing this is gonna get boring fast. Rewatching it, I almost felt like I would've preferred to see more enemies plus setting the abilities on a time-countdown rather than being tied to feeding. Because there was nothing tactical going on there (obviously since there are so few tools available and the enemies were all melee-oriented), it's more about the spectacle than anything else and so at that point why not have the character do these dashes every couple of seconds, for example? And you are playing an Elder after all with additional special abilities like telekinesis.<br /> <br /> Another big problem, though, is that this game is absolutely not reflective of what V5 focuses on. So an issue I see here is people who buy this game and think this is what it's like to play V5 and then they join an online-group or pick up the corebook and then find out that the TTRPG is very different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T14:47:20-08:00","id":1529771,"title":"","content":"I'm happier to play an awakened Elder than a Thin-blood. Shame if its going down heavy on the combat path but we'll see what the end results will be before I cast my judgement on this.<br /> <br /> As long as, whatever they do, they do it well I'm not having a problem with it. A good action game will beat a bad social interaction game.<br /> <br /> Besides even if the game just works as a good plattform for mods I would be content with that. Many games have been &quot;just&quot; good but served as the foundation for awesome modding communities which have elevated the experience far above the original game. I am here thinking about, for example, Medieval: Total War and Mount &amp; Blade: Warbands and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529426#post1529426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole &quot;action brawler&quot; thing is bizarre, given that Bloodlines 2 is a first person game. You'd think they'd be pointing towards other first person games like Cyberpunk or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been very good action focused games with a 1st person perspective. Just all the FPS games and the melee focused game Vermintide shows its perfectly doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":".  Added the quote and a comment 01-31-2024, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T15:13:15-08:00","id":1529772,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines also had a shit ton of combat and stealth.<br /> <br /> People just forget this unless they think of the sewers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T15:15:05-08:00","id":1529773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529771#post1529771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There have been very good action focused games with a 1st person perspective. Just all the FPS games and the melee focused game Vermintide shows its perfectly doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are indeed quite a few first-person action-games. Cyberpunk also has a lot of RPG in its DNA. The game you mentioned Vermintide is another (or Darktide for the WH40k variant) but those are also team-based games. Since we're talking single-player, I think the better comparison would be Ghostrunner or Shadow Warrior (I think those two I would set as milestones for how close Bloodlines 2 in its action-gameplay gets to that level). But you can have good first-person action in a game, like you said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T18:50:44-08:00","id":1529794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529771#post1529771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There have been very good action focused games with a 1st person perspective. Just all the FPS games and the melee focused game Vermintide shows its perfectly doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I just found it weird that Chinese room is pointing towards 3rd person melee focused action games instead of other 1st person melee focused action games, given that Bloodlines 2 is a 1st person game, not a 3rd person one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T23:06:48-08:00","id":1529804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529772#post1529772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines also had a shit ton of combat and stealth.<br /> <br /> People just forget this unless they think of the sewers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very much true. Especially when considering how the second half of the game kind of descends into a combat slog with combat mission after combat mission.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529794#post1529794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I just found it weird that Chinese room is pointing towards 3rd person melee focused action games instead of other 1st person melee focused action games, given that Bloodlines 2 is a 1st person game, not a 3rd person one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such is true. I suppose we'll have to wait to and see how it turns out. But as long as the game can support extensive modding I think we'll survive a base game which may just be about &quot;ok&quot;. Or so I hope. Sometimes I wish they could call it something else than &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot; as that links the game to the previous game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T02:45:07-08:00","id":1529809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529772#post1529772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines also had a shit ton of combat and stealth.<br /> <br /> People just forget this unless they think of the sewers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what you need to take into account here is that when people talk lovingly of their experience with Bloodlines 1, they aren't talking about combat and stealth. It was the roleplaying-aspect, the many varied characters, the side-quests, the multiple ways one could deal with various quests and characters. It's the sort of stuff that also makes Baldurs Gate 3 great. So rather than just the emphasis on combat and stealth which people are complaining about, it's the feeling that this is a far more linear game.<br /> <br /> Personally, I made my peace with this game not offering the same kind of roleplaying-depth as BL1 but I also wouldn't fault anyone for feeling disappointed due to this change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T06:35:43-08:00","id":1529813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529809#post1529809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think what you need to take into account here is that when people talk lovingly of their experience with Bloodlines 1, they aren't talking about combat and stealth. It was the roleplaying-aspect, the many varied characters, the side-quests, the multiple ways one could deal with various quests and characters. It's the sort of stuff that also makes Baldurs Gate 3 great. So rather than just the emphasis on combat and stealth which people are complaining about, it's the feeling that this is a far more linear game.<br /> <br /> Personally, I made my peace with this game not offering the same kind of roleplaying-depth as BL1 but I also wouldn't fault anyone for feeling disappointed due to this change.</div> </div> </div> </div>My response, though, is they're not showing that element yet because this is the combat trailer.<br /> <br /> This is the trailer for the people who play combat driven video games.<br /> <br /> Also, the primary complaint about the original Bloodlines 2 trailers was how janky the combat looked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T07:14:25-08:00","id":1529814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529813#post1529813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My response, though, is they're not showing that element yet because this is the combat trailer.<br /> <br /> This is the trailer for the people who play combat driven video games.<br /> <br /> Also, the primary complaint about the original Bloodlines 2 trailers was how janky the combat looked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the problem. They did mention &quot;social feeding&quot;, so there is some sort of non-combat section gameplay. But we have yet to see that in action. I assume it's because this is yet another thing that's still deep in development and mostly unfinished. Like how it's still impossible to show off Ventrue-abilities apparently.<br /> <br /> Or even worse: I think it's absolutely insane that we have yet to see or hear the male version of Phyre. That voice-actor is of equal importance to the female Phyre-voice-actor and yet somehow that voice-actor's work never got shown in the previews thus far.<br /> <br /> If this trailer had been released last October we'd be in a very different place. At least this gives off the impression of a finished game. But it's still one of those &quot;vertical slices&quot; that are often used very disingenuously by videogame-companies these days. And since the previous previews were so lackluster it created trepidations about the quality of this game that this new trailer didn't entirely dispel. Why revisit a scene we've already seen two times before? The only way I can explain it is that similar to last Fall, they simply <i>can't</i> show something else off because it's too deep in development. That isn't good.<br /> <br /> As long as the roleplaying-depth hasn't been shown in gameplay, it's baseless to claim BL2 has anything like that. And the gameplay-trailer we got had nothing like a roleplaying-oriented moment but instead dialogue-options that led to two outcomes &quot;Willem blows himself up - or not.&quot; The rest was meaningless. Like you'd find in a Bioware-game where it has this hourglass-approach to its story-design. You have all these options, and make all these choices but at some point, it all just gets funneled into the only meaningful part which was often just an &quot;either/or&quot;-thing like &quot;Did you kill the character or let him escape&quot;. But the particular dialogue-options you had chosen to get to that point weren't important.<br /> <br /> And I mean, yeah, the game-play looked better than previous previews but like I said: Compared to other games in the genre it's mid to disappointing at best. A lot of &quot;been there, done that&quot;-stuff and a severe lack of options in the gameplay that could spice things up. Again, I think the fundamental issue here is that this game is limited by how little of the game has been finished so far. Of course, you can't show off what you don't have.<br /> <br /> Also, again, the main-interest for fans of BL1 is roleplaying-depth. Rolling out previews that don't focus on that doesn't inspire confidence that this game does have roleplaying-depth. This counterproductive PR-strategy understandably leads to disappointment among fans of BL1 in this regard. The first impression so far has been that it's less interested in roleplaying and more interested in combat. But that's the fault of the previews and not the fans who feel disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T07:52:10-08:00","id":1529816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529814#post1529814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's the problem. They did mention &quot;social feeding&quot;, so there is some sort of non-combat section gameplay. But we have yet to see that in action. I assume it's because this is yet another thing that's still deep in development and mostly unfinished. Like how it's still impossible to show off Ventrue-abilities apparently.<br /> <br /> Or even worse: I think it's absolutely insane that we have yet to see or hear the male version of Phyre. That voice-actor is of equal importance to the female Phyre-voice-actor and yet somehow that voice-actor's work never got shown in the previews thus far.<br /> <br /> If this trailer had been released last October we'd be in a very different place. At least this gives off the impression of a finished game. But it's still one of those &quot;vertical slices&quot; that are often used very disingenuously by videogame-companies these days. And since the previous previews were so lackluster it created trepidations about the quality of this game that this new trailer didn't entirely dispel. Why revisit a scene we've already seen two times before? The only way I can explain it is that similar to last Fall, they simply <i>can't</i> show something else off because it's too deep in development. That isn't good.<br /> <br /> As long as the roleplaying-depth hasn't been shown in gameplay, it's baseless to claim BL2 has anything like that. And the gameplay-trailer we got had nothing like a roleplaying-oriented moment but instead dialogue-options that led to two outcomes &quot;Willem blows himself up - or not.&quot; The rest was meaningless. Like you'd find in a Bioware-game where it has this hourglass-approach to its story-design. You have all these options, and make all these choices but at some point, it all just gets funneled into the only meaningful part which was often just an &quot;either/or&quot;-thing like &quot;Did you kill the character or let him escape&quot;. But the particular dialogue-options you had chosen to get to that point weren't important.<br /> <br /> And I mean, yeah, the game-play looked better than previous previews but like I said: Compared to other games in the genre it's mid to disappointing at best. A lot of &quot;been there, done that&quot;-stuff and a severe lack of options in the gameplay that could spice things up. Again, I think the fundamental issue here is that this game is limited by how little of the game has been finished so far. Of course, you can't show off what you don't have.<br /> <br /> Also, again, the main-interest for fans of BL1 is roleplaying-depth. Rolling out previews that don't focus on that doesn't inspire confidence that this game does have roleplaying-depth. This counterproductive PR-strategy understandably leads to disappointment among fans of BL1 in this regard. The first impression so far has been that it's less interested in roleplaying and more interested in combat. But that's the fault of the previews and not the fans who feel disappointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess I'm taking this view from the perspective this is meant to show off how the combat system works and how the graphics have improved. This isn't the social element of the game meant to sell the game to longtime V:TM fans but an attempt to sell this to the casual gamer who want to play an action game. They had a lot of hype at the start of this with Hardsuit Labs but that ended up being torpedoed. Now they have to appeal to the largest possible audience who isn't necessarily V:TM or Bloodlines fans.<br /> <br /> Fans of Bloodlines are not looking for how to see how the social element works and the characters but that isn't th part this is focused on. We get a few choices but this is a &quot;social boss&quot; fight like the kind in Deus Ex: Human Revolution where you talk down a guy who is holding a person hostage at the start of the game.<br /> <br /> The game could have huge chunks of social interaction and storytelling but it's not in the combat level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T08:26:51-08:00","id":1529817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529816#post1529816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now they have to appeal to the largest possible audience who isn't necessarily V:TM or Bloodlines fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why BL1 fans are disappointed. The focus is getting watered down. And &quot;appealing to the largest possible audience&quot; is a management-aspiration, not a game-concept. This is how publishers ruin videogames.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529816#post1529816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fans of Bloodlines are not looking for how to see how the social element works and the characters but that isn't th part this is focused on.</div> </div> </div> </div>They absolutely are looking to find out more about the social and roleplaying elements. And that there's no gameplay-footage to inspire confidence in this being done well or at all creates the disappointment a lot of BL1 fans are feeling at the moment. To them that was the best part of BL1 and the previews so far haven't shown off any of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529816#post1529816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We get a few choices but this is a &quot;social boss&quot; fight like the kind in Deus Ex: Human Revolution where you talk down a guy who is holding a person hostage at the start of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! That game's a horrible example! That game famously was criticized for its unavoidable boss-battles which you could only solve via shooting/punching the boss to death. It was only after the uproar that the Director's Cut was later introduced which added more options to the boss-fights.<br /> <br /> Also, that wasn't a &quot;boss-fight&quot;. The main-component which decided the fate of Willem is the dialogue-options. No matter what you said when you first meet Willem, you end up in this scenario. Then in the combat you just beat the crap out of the enemies until a certain number is reached and in the dialogue-tree the only thing that matters is &quot;Did you choose the options that keep Willem from blowing himself up or not?&quot;. Any &quot;roleplaying&quot; is purely aesthetical here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524819-vampire-bloodlines-update?p=1529816#post1529816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game could have huge chunks of social interaction and storytelling but it's not in the combat level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, which is a baseless claim at this point. Talk is cheap. Especially when it comes to videogame-previews.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T11:06:14-08:00","id":1529825,"title":"","content":"I think a useful way to look at the trailer is to borrow a term from TV: it's a &quot;bottle episode.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bottle episodes, for those that don't want to do a quick Google, are when a TV show reuses as much pre-made elements as possible: no special guests, all existing costumes/make-up, all existing sets, etc. While born out of necessity to make some low cost episodes to balance out high cost episodes, they're generally neutral. Bottle episodes can be great, or terrible, because the central premise of the episode and the writing need to be extremely on point without any other spectacle to catch viewer attention.<br /> <br /> The trailer is a mission that uses many of the same tricks: limited cast, reusing the same map over and over to limit how many digital assets they need to employ, etc. It's not inherently bad, especially as we lack the greater context of the story.<br /> <br /> The problem is that video game consumers are very burnt out on deceptive trailers (and really have been for decades at this point). &quot;Bottle episode&quot; tricks are a staple of this: refine one low asset preview to the point where it looks great, but offer no real look at what the world outside that wonderful little bottle is really like.<br /> <br /> We can see things like the traversal mechanics (walking, running, jumping, clambering, gliding from the looks of it) all working really well... in that curated warehouse map. Is every map well detailed and considered, or is a lot of travel going to feel unrefined and janky once your in larger world sections or just less refined level map? We don't know. But a lot of video game fans have seen time and time again than these smooth actions in trailers and previews don't make it into the final product because most of the game isn't going to get the fine-toothed comb treatment to show that off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T19:02:00-08:00","id":1529842,"title":"","content":"Very much in the wait and see camp for this. But at 4:20 in the gameplay trailer Willem rushes Phyre and grabs her before she can react, is that Celerity or maybe just blood buff? I worry that they've given every kindred superhuman attributes which sorta waters down the physical disciplines. I know Potence or Celerity 1 is so easy to get anyone can have it but its worth mentioning after seeing a Nos have super speed in a cut-scene like that. I'm purposely ignoring the weird screech/moan thing he does right afterwards<br /> <br /> edit: also in the Tremere reveal where they punch a dude and he goes flying into a wall is what made me first notice this trend with the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug","user":"abugintherug","date":". 02-02-2024, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug","name":"abugintherug","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28284_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-0